@{
    Layout = "/Views/Shared/_Layout.cshtml";
}

@section HeaderImage
{
    <div class="headerImage2">
        <img src="~/images/talenmt-scouting.png" />
    </div>
}
<div class="hometext">
    <p class="paraCommon" style="text-align:center">
        <img src="/images/talentscoutig2.png" width="50%" />
    </p>
    <div class="">
        <p class="paraCommon paraHeader"> <b>Scouting Talent; Clarity attracts faster than ads</b> 
            <span style="font-size:20px">Modern talent doesn’t respond to noise; they respond to purpose</span>
        </p>

        <p class="paraCommon">Most companies still throw mass job ads into the ocean and pray something bites.  </p>
        <p class="paraCommon">Today’s green workforce reads that as “we don’t know who we want.” </p>
        <p class="paraCommon">Fresh thinking flips the model: <i>clarity first, channels later.</i> </p>
        <p class="paraCommon"><b>When companies articulate sincerity, purpose, culture, and learning freedom up front, the right candidates appear faster, because talent is already scouting you while you think you’re scouting them.</b> </p>
        <p class="paraCommon">The time has come when scouting talent needs to shift from Fishing Nets to Laser Targeting. Most companies still chase candidates with mass job posts. </p>
        <p class="paraCommon"><b>Green employers flip the script, they define who they are before defining<i> who they need</i> . When your purpose, culture, and intent are sharp, right candidates spot you first.</b></p>
        <p class="paraCommon">This isn’t “sourcing.” This is <b>self-selection</b> at its finest.</p>
        <p class="paraCommon">Click Here to Participate in Talent Scouting Poll
            <a href="/visitor/poll/50" class="homeImage"><img src="~/images/audience-poll.png" width="70px" /></a>
        </p>
    </div>
</div>
